{"ts": 1791258164.016603, "type": "step", "step": 16, "action": "messages_read_channel", "args": {"channel": "dm:student"}, "output": "[t=-10] student: hey, I started the writeup but I'm stuck on the eval part\n[t=0] agent: You\u2019re on the right topic: for this build, the key eval distinction is probably **pass^k**. That means the solution must succeed on **all k runs**, not just one. A quick way to write it up is: define what you\u2019re measuring, say why direct reliability matters, and contrast it with any proxy metric you used. If you paste the eval paragraph you\u2019ve drafted, I can help tighten it.\n[t=0] student: nice, I think I see it now", "t": 4, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20282525443759936, "pomdp": 0.20282525443759936, "pass_k": 0.3691804618986463}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7843091835012588, "motivation": 0.8589364796632395, "reliance": 0.45602770298460465, "persistence": 0.37480768876559933, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3439719309903426, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2920196205727638, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
